  "items": [
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3myjcs6g7zc2q",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "By every measure, Opus 4.8 beats human experts as peer reviewers in a study of 124 Harvard social science papers covering a range from statistical analyses to formal models to qualitative work.\n\nAs academics, we need to figure out how to adapt the practice of science to AI, and we need to do it fast",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3myjcs6g7zc2q",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-23T04:12:29.185Z",
      "likes": 193,
      "replies": 13,
      "reposts": 43,
      "score": 7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.4,
        "recency": 0.7,
        "age_hours": 44.6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mykox5d5k22o",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "As the gap between the internal models at the AI labs and the ones they release grow (due to safety concerns & research advantages), it will be increasingly tempting for OpenAI & Anthropic to exploit that advantage directly by entering new markets, especially in finance & biotech.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mykox5d5k22o",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-23T17:22:40.447Z",
      "likes": 87,
      "replies": 15,
      "reposts": 10,
      "score": 6.7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.1,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 31.4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mygfwzgdc22g",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "A visible sign of what AI insiders have been warning about since at least the Mythos release. Acceleration of attack and defense, at inhuman speeds, interacting with the very human systems that need to react to them.\n\nAnd these are the vulnerabilities we know about.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mygfwzgdc22g",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-22T00:30:53.724Z",
      "likes": 164,
      "replies": 4,
      "reposts": 30,
      "score": 6.3,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.3,
        "recency": 0.6,
        "age_hours": 72.3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:uvsuoi63hmxbr35fmozsghpc/app.bsky.feed.post/3myl3lpwkqc2h",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "Excited to announce that I'll be keynoting at Black Hat Europe this year in London! I'll be talking about the distinction between AI Security and AI Safety, and the co-option and conflation of security and safety methodologies in AI that are leading us down a precarious path.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3myl3lpwkqc2h",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-23T21:08:55.948Z",
      "likes": 24,
      "replies": 0,
      "reposts": 7,
      "score": 5.5,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.5,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 27.6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3myldyolep226",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "Been saying OpenAI needs to train on a simulation of the internet instead of the real internet techcrunch.com/2026/10/23/o...",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3myldyolep226",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-23T23:39:20.672Z",
      "likes": 16,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 3,
      "score": 5.3,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.4,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 25.1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3mylmyrsus226",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "There is a lot of interest from all the big AI labs on character steering, personas, etc. including Anthropic. I think it is poorly understood. @natolambert.bsky.social could probably say more. I’m not sure the Claude persona was intentional, but it is sort of a brand at this point, Ala Claudisms.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3mylmyrsus226",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-24T02:20:27.741Z",
      "likes": 8,
